  "rationale": "Direct-match candidates are present for sleep apnea, including multiple generic “Sleep apnea” scores from the ExPRSweb framework (PGS003204–PGS003218) and multiple disease-focused obstructive sleep apnea (OSA) scores (PGS003857/PGS003858, PGS005219/PGS005220). Domain knowledge states OSA is the clinically dominant form of sleep apnea, so OSA models are acceptable/preferred direct matches when better supported. Among the OSA candidates, PGS005220 (Obstructive sleep apnea, UnadjustedBMI) comes from a disease-focused publication and reports higher discrimination than the ExPRSweb sleep-apnea cluster (full-model AUROC 0.79 vs ~0.49–0.53) without explicit BMI-adjusted endpoint labeling, making it the cleaner choice for generic sleep apnea risk than the BMI-adjusted variants. However, confidence is limited because the reported AUROC is a full-model metric (not PGS-only/incremental), covariates include BMI (a major mediator/risk factor that can inflate full-model AUROC), and key training details are listed as N/A, so PRS-only contribution and comparability remain unclear."
}
